{'symbol': 'TGT', 'date': '2020-01-15 10:30:00', 'title': 'Target Reports Holiday Sales And Maintains EPS Guidance', 'text': "TARGET REPORTS HOLIDAY SALES AND MAINTAINS EPS GUIDANCE.TARGET CORP - COMPARABLE DIGITAL SALES GREW 19 PERCENT IN NOVEMBER/DECEMBER PERIOD.TARGET CORP -  SALES THROUGH TARGET'S SAME-DAY FULFILLMENT SERVICES GREW MORE THAN 50 PERCENT FROM NOVEMBER/DECEMBER PERIOD LAST YEAR.TARGET CORP - NOW EXPECTS Q4 COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH IN LINE WITH ITS NOVEMBER/DECEMBER PERFORMANCE OF 1.4 PERCENT.TARGET CORP -  COMP SALES GROWTH IN  NOVEMBER/DECEMBER PERIOD DRIVEN PRIMARILY BY TRAFFIC, COMBINED WITH A SMALL INCREASE IN AVERAGE TICKET.TARGET - FACED CHALLENGES THROUGHOUT NOVEMBER AND DECEMBER IN KEY SEASONAL MERCHANDISE CATEGORIES AND OUR HOLIDAY SALES DID NOT MEET OUR EXPECTATIONS.TARGET CORP - ANNOUNCED RETIREMENT OF EXECUTIVE VICE PRESIDENT AND CHIEF STORES OFFICER JANNA POTTS.TARGET CORP - MARK SCHINDELE HAS BEEN NAMED EXECUTIVE VICE PRESIDENT AND CHIEF STORES OFFICER.TARGET CORP - FORMALIZING INTERIM STRUCTURE IT ANNOUNCED FOR ITS MERCHANDISING ORGANIZATION IN OCTOBER.TARGET CORP SEES FULL-YEAR 2019 COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH OF MORE THAN 3 PERCENT.TARGET - IN HOLIDAY PERIOD,  STRENGTH IN MANY CATEGORIES OFFSET BY SOFTER-THAN-EXPECTED PERFORMANCE IN KEY HOLIDAY CATEGORIES.TARGET - SOFTER-THAN-EXPECTED PERFORMANCE IN ELECTRONICS, TOYS, PORTIONS OF HOME, WHICH TOGETHER ACCOUNT FOR ABOUT ONE-THIRD OF HOLIDAY SEASON SALES.TARGET CORP - HAVE SEEN CONTINUED STRENGTH AND MARKET SHARE GAINS IN APPAREL, BEAUTY, ESSENTIALS AND FOOD & BEVERAGE IN HOLIDAY SEASON."}
